---
import Layout from "@layouts/ComponentsLayout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Inset text</h1>
  <p class="govuk-body-l">
    Use the inset text component to differentiate a block of text from the
    content that surrounds it
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Example</h2>
  <div class="govuk-inset-text">
    It can take up to 8 weeks to register a lasting power of attorney if there
    are no mistakes in the application.
  </div>

  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:START (auto-generated - edited content will be overwritten by scripts/update-component-guidance.mjs) -->
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">When to use this component</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the inset text component to differentiate a block of text from the
    content that surrounds it, for example:
  </p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>quotes</li>
    <li>examples</li>
    <li>additional information about the page</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">When not to use this component</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Some users do not notice inset text if it’s used on complex pages or near to
    other visually prominent elements. For this reason, avoid using inset text
    as a way of highlighting very important information that users need to see.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you need to draw attention to very important content, like legal
    information, use the <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/warning-text/"
      >Warning text component</a
    > instead.
  </p>
  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:END -->
</Layout>
